{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: the original model placed the prior `beta ~ normal(0, 10)` on `beta`, a transformed parameter derived from the top-level parameter `beta_tilde`. SafeStan requires priors to be sampling statements on top-level parameters. The safe version uses the equivalent QR parameterization with `beta` as the top-level parameter and defines `beta_tilde = R * beta` as a transformed parameter. This preserves the regression likelihood and the intended prior on `beta` while satisfying SafeStan's parameter-prior discipline. The data file is unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  int<lower=1> M;
  matrix[M, N] X;
  vector[N] y;
}

transformed data {
  matrix[M, N] X_centered;
  matrix[N, M] Q;
  matrix[M, M] R;
  matrix[M, M] R_inv;

  for (m in 1:M)
    X_centered[m] = X[m] - mean(X[m]);

  // Compute, thin, and then scale QR decomposition
   Q = qr_Q(X_centered')[, 1:M] * N;
   R = qr_R(X_centered')[1:M, ] / N;
   R_inv = inverse(R);
}

parameters {
  vector[M] beta;
  real alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}

transformed parameters {
  vector[M] beta_tilde = R * beta;
}

model {
  beta ~ normal(0, 10);
  alpha ~ normal(0, 100);
  sigma ~ cauchy(0, 10);

  y ~ normal(Q * beta_tilde + alpha, sigma);
}
